  "report_period": "Week 32 (6th Aug to 13th Aug 2021)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "The Capesize \"Aqua Splendor\" 175/2012 Jinhai, China (SS/DD 06/2022) was sold to undisclosed buyers for mid-high USD 20's mill. Note you that a month ago, the one-year-older \"Mangas\" 174/2011 Bohai, China (SS 03/2026, DD 05/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 24 mill. Safe Bulkers have committed their Panamax \"Lemessos Queen\" 76/2008 Imabari, Japan (SS 10/2023, DD 10/2021, BWTS fitted) to Middle Eastern buyers for mid-high USD 18 mill. For comparison, the one-year-older \"Canea\" 75/2007 Universal, Japan (SS/DD 06/2022) was sold a couple of weeks ago at USD 17,5 mill. Vietnamese buyers have acquired two Ultramax sister vessels, the \"Lowlands Beacon\" 61/2011 Iwagi, Japan (SS/DD 04/2022) from Hisamoto Kisen for USD 21 mill & the two-years-younger \"Santa Barbara\" 61/2013 Iwagi, Japan (SS/DD 01/2023) from Konlink Shipping for USD 24,5 mill. Remind you that the sister vessel \"New Aspiration\" 61/2011 Iwagi, Japan (SS/DD 10/2021, BWTS fitted) was sold three weeks ago at USD 21 mill. On the Supramax sector, the \"Aditya\" 55/2008 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 02/2023) was sold for USD 16,5 mill basis delivery September-October 2021, while the two-years-younger \"Dory\" 55/2010 IHI, Japan (SS 09/2025, DD 04/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold a couple of weeks ago at USD 17,5 mill. Japanese owners have sold their Handysize \"Ocean Mercury\" 37/2012 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 03/2025, DD 03/2023) for mid USD 13 mill with T/C attached until May 2022 at 9.000 usd/pd, whilst the Japanese built \"Maratha Promise\" 37/2012 Saiki, Japan (SS/DD 03/2022) of Chowgule Steamships was committed for USD 16,5 mill. In addition, the OHBS \"Sakura Kobe\" 33/2011 Shin Kochi, Japan (SS 11/2024, DD 10/2022, BWTS fitted) was sold to Hong Kong based buyers Taylor Maritime for USD 16,2 mill.",
    "tankers": "Thang Long Gas have sold their VLCC \"Maya Vn\" 318/2003 Hyundai Samho, Korea (SS 04/2023, DD 08/2021, Ldt: 44.131) to Chinese buyers for USD 27 mill. Note that the vessel was acquired a month ago at demo levels 560 usd/ldt basis \"As Is\" Batam including 600T of bunkers ROB. For comparison reasons, the \"Olympic Legend\" 309/2003 Samsung, Korea (SS/DD 09/2023) was sold back in July for USD 31 mill. The Aframax \"Jag Lata\" 105/2003 Hyundai Samho, Korea (SS/DD 05/2023) from Great Eastern Shipping was committed to Chinese buyers for USD 13,5 mill. Remind you that the \"Astro Saturn\" 105/2003 Daewoo, Korea (SS 04/2023, DD 08/2021) was sold a couple of weeks ago at USD 12,4 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of low/mid usd 14,00's fio range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "CIS Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 25,000/26,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 30,000/31,000 pd range. A number of Australian trips into China were fixed around usd 31,000/32,000 pd. South East Asian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 33,000/34,000 pd. Indian trips via Black Sea into China were fixed around usd 33,000/34,000 pd. Inter- Continental trips via Baltic were reported at the level of usd 30,000 pd. On the period front, a Kamsarmax were reported fixed in the usd 18,250 pd for 2 years employment basis delivery in the Pacific.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 30,000/32,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 32,000/35,000 pd range. Indian trips via South Africa into South East Asia were reported at the level of usd 38,000 pd. Persian Gulf trips into India were fixed around usd 44,000/45,000 pd. South African trips into China were reported at the level of usd 32,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 1.1M. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "A number of trips from Japan into Thailand with steels were fixed around usd 40,000 pd. A number of Australian trips into China with spodumene were reported at the level of usd 40,000 pd. Indian trips via Persian Gulf into US Gulf were fixed around usd 34,000/35,000 pd. Persian Gulf trips into India were reported around usd 43,000 pd. Continental and Mediterranean trips into US Gulf were fixed at the level of usd 37,000/39,000 pd. Continental trips into Mediterranean were fixed around usd 30,000/32,000 pd. South American trips into ARAG were reported at the level of usd 31,000/33,000 pd. A small Handysize was fixed on period at the usd 32,500 pd basis delivery Mediterranean for3/5 months employment with redelivery Atlantic."
    }
  },
